    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0574" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.38/53.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-12T10:00:00-04:49">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1915—10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Haitian Senate ratified the treaty last night. The vote was, in favor 25,
                    against 9, chairman of the Senate committee not voting. I am informed by the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs that the Haitian Government will submit for
                    signature in a few days a modus vivendi embodying the terms of the treaty and
                    that the appointment of the commission to proceed to Washington is now being
                    considered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
